# spec: the 700 takes names the Bose app accepts, at most 26 bytes of UTF-8; 14 "é" are 28 bytes, so the library refuses the name and sends nothing.
# source: the Bose app's validateProductName (byte limit 26), and the owner of a 700 seeing 14 "é" refused as too long in the Bose app
device nc700
call set_name éééééééééééééé
result err invalid-arg
